      "audit_status": "source_checked"
    },
    {
      "id": "011000-e02",
      "anchor": "A thermostable polymerase derived from Thermus aquaticus, commonly called Taq polymerase, made repeated cycles practical without replacing the enzyme each time.",
      "kind": "evidence_and_history",
      "source_ids": [
        "lw-extreme-nps-pcr"
      ],
      "source_locator": "Taq polymerase PCR",
      "audit_status": "source_checked"
    },
    {
      "id": "011000-e03",
      "anchor": "In 1971, Arthur DeVries reported that glycoproteins in the blood of Antarctic fish produced a separation between the temperature at which a fluid would begin to freeze and the temperature at which ice would melt.",
      "kind": "evidence_and_history",
      "source_ids": [
        "lw-extreme-devries1971"
      ],
      "source_locator": "Antifreeze glycoprotein discovery",
      "audit_status": "source_checked"
    },
    {
      "id": "011000-e04",
      "anchor": "Researchers later traced the origin of the Antarctic notothenioid antifreeze glycoprotein system to a rearrangement and modification involving an ancestral trypsinogen gene.",
      "kind": "evidence_and_history",
      "source_ids": [
        "lw-extreme-chen1997"
      ],
      "source_locator": "Antifreeze gene evolution",
      "audit_status": "source_checked"
    },
    {
      "id": "011000-e05",
      "anchor": "Concentrated urine and relatively dry feces reduce losses through excretion.",
      "kind": "evidence_and_history",
      "source_ids": [
        "lw-extreme-nps-rats"
      ],
      "source_locator": "Kangaroo rat water conservation",
      "audit_status": "source_checked"
    },
    {
      "id": "011000-e06",
      "anchor": "In 2014, Paul Yancey and colleagues measured high TMAO concentrations in hadal snailfish from around seven thousand meters deep, extending measurements of a trend in which TMAO increases with depth in some marine fishes.",
      "kind": "evidence_and_history",
      "source_ids": [
        "lw-extreme-yancey2014"
      ],
      "source_locator": "TMAO measurement",
      "audit_status": "source_checked"
    },
    {
      "id": "011000-e07",
      "anchor": "Experiments reported in 2017 indicated that tardigrade-specific intrinsically disordered proteins contribute to desiccation tolerance, and some protected other cells when expressed there.",
      "kind": "evidence_and_history",
      "source_ids": [
